## Context

Flagged by the 0403 worker's sweep (PR #738): 0403 unified FP bars to
red (COLOR_ALERT) across the **Exp2** figures, but the Exp1 main-text
figure `fig_direct_p1_base.pdf` (produced by
`aedist.plot_method_convergence`) still draws its FP segments orange.
The repo convention after 0403 is: false positives are red, labeled
"unrecognized" (never "hallucinated").

## Quoi faire

1. `src/aedist/plot_method_convergence.py`: FP segments → COLOR_ALERT
   red. Note its "Hallucinations" text label was judged a legitimate
   non-FP-bar use in the 0403 sweep — re-examine: if the label names
   the red segments, relabel "unrecognized" per convention.
2. Sweep siblings for remaining orange-FP uses the 0403 Exp2-scoped
   sweep deliberately left (plot_scaling_curve.py reference line was
   judged legitimate — confirm).
3. Regression test mirroring tests/test_plot_exp2_arms_comparison.py.
4. REBUILD the committed PDF after the change (stale-PDF trap); check
   any caption naming the colour (report + manuscript).

## Exit criteria

- [x] fig_direct_p1_base FP segments red; label says "unrecognized"
- [x] Regression test green (red on revert)
- [x] PDF regenerated post-fix and committed; captions consistent
